<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Default test settings for Bosun (bs-ef4).

  TestCaseFilter excludes the Integration category so that a bare "dotnet test" — the thing
  everyone types, and the thing an agent types without thinking — CANNOT reach a real rclone rcd,
  WinFsp, a drive letter, or the real Windows Terminal fragment path.

  Safety before convenience: Bosun mounts real drive letters, and one pointing at an unreachable
  host blocks Explorer, "dir", and file dialogs process-wide across the OS (Invariant I2,
  ADR-005). Opting in to that is a deliberate act, and requires the sibling settings file:

      dotnet test                                            -> safe; excludes Integration
      dotnet test [settings] integration.runsettings         -> explicit opt-in

  NOTE, verified empirically rather than assumed: a filter passed on the COMMAND LINE is ANDed
  with the TestCaseFilter below, not substituted for it. Asking for "Category=Integration" that
  way produces "(Category!=Integration)&(Category=Integration)" and silently matches NOTHING —
  it looks like a clean run rather than an error. Supply integration.runsettings instead, which
  replaces these settings outright.
-->
<RunSettings>
  <RunConfiguration>
    <TestCaseFilter>Category!=Integration</TestCaseFilter>
  </RunConfiguration>
</RunSettings>
